# 7) Backend API example

Your server should support:

- `POST /surveys` → create survey, return `{ id }`
- `PUT /surveys/:id` → update survey
- `DELETE /surveys/:id` → delete survey
- optionally `GET /surveys/changes?since=timestamp` → pull server updates

Example Express server:

## `server.js`

```js
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

const surveys = new Map();

app.post('/surveys', (req, res) => {
  const id = String(Date.now());
  surveys.set(id, { id, ...req.body });
  res.json({ id });
});

app.put('/surveys/:id', (req, res) => {
  const id = req.params.id;
  surveys.set(id, { id, ...req.body });
  res.json({ ok: true });
});

app.delete('/surveys/:id', (req, res) => {
  const id = req.params.id;
  surveys.delete(id);
  res.json({ ok: true });
});

app.get('/surveys', (req, res) => {
  res.json([...surveys.values()]);
});

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('API running on 3000'));
```

