# 10) Minimal backend logic

Pseudo-code for server-side conflict handling:

```ts
app.post("/sync/upload", async (req, res) => {
  const { operations } = req.body;
  const conflicts = [];

  for (const op of operations) {
    const serverEntity = await db.findById(op.entityType, op.entityId);

    if (serverEntity && op.payload.version <= serverEntity.version) {
      conflicts.push({
        entityType: op.entityType,
        entityId: op.entityId,
        reason: "Version conflict",
        serverValue: serverEntity,
      });
      continue;
    }

    await db.upsert(op.entityType, op.payload);
  }

  res.json({
    success: conflicts.length === 0,
    conflicts,
    nextSyncToken: await generateSyncToken(),
  });
});
```

