## 8) Important note: enabling/disabling rules dynamically

The popup currently stores an `enabled` flag, but the blocking rules are always active. In a more complete MV3 implementation, you would use:

- `chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets()`

to enable or disable the ruleset based on the toggle.

For example, you can add this to `background.js`:

```js
async function setBlockingEnabled(enabled) {
  await chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets({
    enableRulesetIds: enabled ? ["core_rules"] : [],
    disableRulesetIds: enabled ? [] : ["core_rules"]
  });
}

chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async () => {
  const defaults = { enabled: true, blockedCount: 0 };
  const current = await chrome.storage.local.get(Object.keys(defaults));
  const merged = { ...defaults, ...current };
  await chrome.storage.local.set(merged);
  await setBlockingEnabled(merged.enabled);
});

chrome.storage.onChanged.addListener(async (changes, area) => {
  if (area === "local" && changes.enabled) {
    await setBlockingEnabled(changes.enabled.newValue);
  }
});
```

