## 3) How to replace simulated data with real live updates

If you later have a WebSocket feed, replace `updatePrices()` with something like:

```js
const ws = new WebSocket("wss://your-feed.example.com");

ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const message = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // Example message:
  // { symbol: "AAPL", price: 212.34 }

  const s = stocks.find(d => d.symbol === message.symbol);
  if (s) {
    s.prevPrice = s.price;
    s.price = message.price;
    s.changePct = ((s.price - s.prevPrice) / s.prevPrice) * 100;
    draw();
  }
};
