public enum RiskDecision {
    ALLOW,
    REJECT
}
```

### `RiskEngine.java`

```java
package com.example.trading.risk;

import com.example.trading.config.TradingConfig;
import com.example.trading.order.Order;

import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;

public final class RiskEngine {
    private final TradingConfig config;
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, AtomicLong> notionalBySymbol = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public RiskEngine(TradingConfig config) {
        this.config = config;
    }

    public RiskDecision check(Order order, double marketPrice) {
        if (order.quantity <= 0 || order.quantity > config.maxOrderQty) {
            return RiskDecision.REJECT;
        }

        long notional = (long) (order.quantity * marketPrice);
        AtomicLong current = notionalBySymbol.computeIfAbsent(order.symbol, s -> new AtomicLong(0));
        long projected = current.get() + notional;

        if (projected > config.maxNotionalPerSymbol) {
            return RiskDecision.REJECT;
        }

        current.addAndGet(notional);
        return RiskDecision.ALLOW;
    }
}
```

> In production, risk should be **deterministic, per-partition, and ideally lock-free** on the hot path.

