# 9. Event bus

Use a lightweight internal event bus first. For low latency, a single-producer/single-consumer or partitioned queue is often enough initially.

```rust
// src/engine/event_bus.rs
use std::sync::mpsc::{Sender, Receiver, channel};

#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub enum Event {
    MarketData(crate::domain::market_data::MarketTick),
    NewOrder(crate::domain::order::Order),
    ExecutionReport(crate::domain::execution::ExecutionReport),
    RiskRejected { order_id: u64, reason: String },
}

pub struct EventBus {
    pub tx: Sender<Event>,
    pub rx: Receiver<Event>,
}

impl EventBus {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        let (tx, rx) = channel();
        Self { tx, rx }
    }
}
```

