# 9) Low-latency improvements to add next

## Networking
- Use async I/O carefully
- Prefer binary protocols where possible
- Avoid JSON in the hot path

## Memory
- Use object pools for frequently created objects
- Reduce allocations
- Reuse buffers

## Concurrency
- Use dedicated threads for feed handlers
- Avoid contention in shared state
- Use sharded maps or actor-style ownership

## Risk and order handling
- Make pre-trade checks synchronous and in-memory
- Keep order state machine explicit
- Add idempotency and deduplication

