## What this gives you

### 1. Sharded routing
Messages are hashed by key into one of N shards, reducing lock contention.

### 2. Non-blocking publish
`Publish()` drops when overloaded, which is common in HFT-style systems where latency matters more than guaranteed delivery.

### 3. Latency monitoring
Each shard tracks end-to-end queue + processing latency using a simple histogram.

### 4. Backpressure option
`PublishBlocking()` allows a caller to wait instead of dropping.

