## A better latency bucket function

If you want to avoid floating point math in the hot path:

```go
func bucketIndex(ns uint64) int {
	if ns == 0 {
		return 0
	}
	idx := 0
	for ns > 1 {
		ns >>= 1
		idx++
	}
	if idx >= 63 {
		return 63
	}
	return idx
}
```

This is slower than ideal too, but avoids float conversion. For maximum performance, use `bits.Len64(ns)`.

```go
import "math/bits"

func bucketIndex(ns uint64) int {
	if ns == 0 {
		return 0
	}
	idx := bits.Len64(ns) - 1
	if idx > 63 {
		return 63
	}
	return idx
}
```

