- watches one log file,
- rotates it when it exceeds a size threshold,
- keeps a fixed number of rotated copies,
- uses **no dynamic allocation**,
- avoids buffering large data in memory,
- can run under strict memory limits.

It is intentionally small and practical rather than feature-rich.

