## Key ideas used

### 1. Fixed timestep
Physics is updated at a constant rate:

```cpp
const float fixedDt = 1.0f / 120.0f;
```

This avoids instability when render FPS changes.

### 2. Accumulator loop
If rendering is slower/faster than physics, the loop catches up:

```cpp
accumulator += frameTime;
while (accumulator >= fixedDt) {
    world.step(fixedDt);
    accumulator -= fixedDt;
}
```

### 3. Semi-implicit Euler
More stable than plain Euler:

```cpp
velocity += acceleration * dt;
position += velocity * dt;
```

### 4. Frame-rate constraint
We cap frame time to prevent a “spiral of death”:

```cpp
frameTime = std::min(frameTime, maxFrameTime);
```

